   "text": "I traced the macrocycle atom by atom from the image and wrote it as a SMILES with ring-closure labels.\n\n**Ring backbone.** Starting at the aryl carbonyl and going around, the ring is:\n\n- para-substituted benzene: C(=O)\u2013C6H4\u2013CH2\u2013S\u2013CH2CH2\u2013C(=O)\n- then N(CH2C(=O)NH2) with its CH2 leading into the next residue\n- four reduced-amide units, each of the form N(acyl)\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH\u2013CH(R)\u2013CH2\u2013, joined in sequence.\n\n**Substituents.** In order around the ring, starting from the aryl carbonyl:\n\n1. Unit 1: the NH is on the carbon bearing CH2Ph (benzyl), and the next N carries a cyclopropylacetyl group.\n2. Unit 2: benzyl again, with a second N-cyclopropylacetyl.\n3. Unit 3: the carbon bears a 4-aminobutyl chain (four CH2 then NH2), and the next N carries a 3-phenylpropanoyl group.\n4. Unit 4: benzyl, and the final N carries CH2C(=O)NH2 and the thioether-linked acyl group.\n\n**Stereochemistry.** All four stereocentres have a wedge to the side chain, with N, H, side chain and CH2N as the neighbours. I assigned each as S by CIP priority (N > CH2N > side chain > H). Written in the order N, H, side chain, CH2N, that corresponds to `[C@@H]`.\n\nI checked that the ring-closure digits are opened and closed correctly. The benzene closure `c1` ends up para to the CH2S carbon.\n\nSMILES: O=C1N[C@@H](Cc2ccccc2)CN(C(=O)CC2CC2)CC(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccccc2)CN(C(=O)CC2CC2)CC(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCN)CN(C(=O)CCc2ccccc2)CC(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccccc2)CN(CC(N)=O)C(=O)CCSCc2ccc1cc2"
